<title>MALAYSIA: Stocks linked to Proton chief suspended.</title>
<headline>Stocks linked to Proton chief suspended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of nine listed companies linked to the chairman and chief executive officer of national carmaker Proton Bhd were suspended on Tuesday at the companies' request, the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>Yahaya Ahmad and his wife were killed in a helicopter crash late on Monday night while on his way to the northern town of Kuala Terengganu, an official at Proton's parent DRB-Hicom confirmed to the national Bernama news agency.  </p>
<p>The stocks suspended are: Perusahaan Otomobil Nasioanal Bhd, Diversified Resources Bhd, Hicom Holdings Bhd, Gadek (Malaysia) Bhd, Golden Pharos Bhd, Kedah Cement Holdings Bhd, Edaran Otomobil Nasioanal, Gadek Capital, and Eastern Pacific.</p>
